**: Convert Firestore patterns to SQL\\n```typescript\\n// Firestore snapshot pattern\\nconst snapshot = await adminDb.collection(\'projects\').get();\\nconst items = snapshot.docs.map(doc => ({ id: doc.id, ...doc.data() }));\\n\\n// SQL pattern\\nconst items = await db.select().from(projects);\\n```\\n\\n**Step 4**: Update pagination\\n```typescript\\n// Firestore pagination\\nif (lastVisibleId) {\\n  const lastDoc = await adminDb.collection(\'projects\').doc(lastVisibleId).get();\\n  query = query.startAfter(lastDoc);\\n}\\n\\n// SQL pagination\\nconst lastId = lastVisibleId ? parseInt(lastVisibleId) : 0;\\n// Then use gt(projects.id, lastId)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🔑 Key Conversions Reference\\n\\n### Common Patterns\\n\\n**Create (INSERT)**:\\n```typescript\\n// Before\\nawait adminDb.collection(\'projects\').add({ title, userId });\\n\\n// After\\nconst result = await db.insert(projects).values({ title, userId }).returning();\\n```\\n\\n**Read Single (SELECT)**:\\n```typescript\\n// Before\\nconst doc = await adminDb.collection(\'projects\').doc(id).get();\\nconst data = doc.data();\\n\\n// After\\nconst result = await db.select().from(projects).where(eq(projects.id, id));\\n```\\n\\n**Read Multiple (SELECT)**:\\n```typescript\\n// Before\\nconst snapshot = await adminDb.collection(\'projects\').where(\'userId\', \'==\', userId).get();\\n\\n// After\\nconst result = await db.select().from(projects).where(eq(projects.userId, userId));\\n```\\n\\n**Update (UPDATE)**:\\n```typescript\\n// Before\\nawait adminDb.collection(\'projects\').doc(id).update(data);\\n\\n// After\\nawait db.update(projects).set(data).where(eq(projects.id, id));\\n```\\n\\n**Delete (DELETE)**:\\n```typescript\\n// Before\\nawait adminDb.collection(\'projects\').doc(id).delete();\\n\\n// After\\nawait db.delete(projects).where(eq(projects.id, id));\\n```\\n\\n**Pagination (ORDER BY + LIMIT)**:\\n```typescript\\n// Before\\nquery.orderBy(\'createdAt\', \'desc\').limit(limit + 1)\\n\\n// After\\nawait db.select().from(projects)\\n  .where(gt(projects.id, lastId))\\n  .orderBy(desc(projects.createdAt))\\n  .limit(limit + 1)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ✅ COMPLETION CHECKLIST\\n\\n### Phase 1: Critical Services\\n- [ ] Fix `projectService.ts`\\n  - [ ] Replace all Firestore queries\\n  - [ ] Test all functions\\n  - [ ] Verify pagination\\n\\n- [ ] Fix `transactionService.ts`\\n  - [ ] Replace all Firestore queries\\n  - [ ] Test all functions\\n  - [ ] Verify pagination\\n\\n- [ ] Fix `generation-service.ts`\\n  - [ ] Replace Firestore insert\\n  - [ ] Verify logging works\\n\\n### Phase 2: API Routes\\n- [ ] Fix `/api/users/[id]/reset-password/route.ts`\\n  - [ ] Implement token-based password reset\\n  - [ ] Store tokens in database\\n  - [ ] Verify email sending\\n\\n- [ ] Fix `/api/admin/users/[id]/reset-password/route.ts`\\n  - [ ] Same as above for admin endpoint\\n\\n### Phase 3: Server Actions\\n- [ ] Fix `src/app/manage-users/actions.ts`\\n  - [ ] Replace Firebase references\\n  - [ ] Update to use new services\\n\\n### Phase 4: Templates & Others\\n- [ ] Complete `templateService.ts`\\n  - [ ] Ensure all template types use PostgreSQL\\n\\n### Phase 5: Cleanup\\n- [ ] Remove all Firebase imports\\n- [ ] Test full auth flow\\n- [ ] Verify no Firebase references remain\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🧪 TESTING STRATEGY\\n\\n**For each service**:\\n1. Write test for each function\\n2. Verify PostgreSQL queries work\\n3. Test error handling\\n4. Test edge cases (empty results, pagination, etc.)\\n\\n**For API routes**:\\n1. Test with valid data\\n2. Test with invalid data\\n3. Test authentication\\n4. Test error responses\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📞 COMMANDS TO FIND REMAINING WORK\\n\\n```bash\\n# Find all Firebase references\\ngrep -r \\"adminDb\\\\|adminAuth\\\\|firebase\\" src/ --include=\\"*.ts\\" --include=\\"*.tsx\\"\\n\\n# Find Firestore patterns\\ngrep -r \\"collection\\\\|\\\\.doc(\\" src/services src/app/api --include=\\"*.ts\\"\\n\\n# Find Firebase imports\\ngrep -r \\"