mented (bcryptjs)\\n✓ No breaking API changes\\n✓ Created comprehensive documentation\\n✓ Ready for Phase 2\\n\\n\\n📈 PROGRESS TRACKING\\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\\n\\nCurrent:     50% (4/15 files) ████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░\\nTarget S1:   75% (8/15 files) ███████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░\\nTarget S2:   90% (11/15 files) █████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░\\nTarget S3:   100% (15/15 files) ████████████████████████████\\n\\nTime Invested So Far: ~2 hours (Phase 1)\\nTime Remaining: 3.5-4 hours (Phase 2)\\nTotal Project: ~6 hours\\n\\n\\n🚀 YOU ARE HERE\\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\\n\\nPhase 1: ✅ COMPLETE - Foundation established\\n           • Core auth working\\n           • All patterns documented\\n           • Ready for Phase 2\\n\\nPhase 2: ⏳ READY TO START - All documentation prepared\\n           • 11 files waiting\\n           • Step-by-step guides created\\n           • Patterns established\\n           • Estimated 3.5-4 hours\\n\\nPhase 3: 📋 PLANNED - Deployment ready\\n           • Documentation updated\\n           • Full testing complete\\n           • Production deployment\\n\\n\\n🎓 WHAT YOU\'VE LEARNED\\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\\n\\n✓ Firebase → PostgreSQL migration patterns\\n✓ Firestore queries → SQL equivalents\\n✓ NextAuth integration for authentication\\n✓ bcryptjs password hashing\\n✓ Drizzle ORM usage\\n✓ Service layer architecture\\n✓ React Query mutations\\n✓ Production-ready patterns\\n\\n\\n📞 WHEN YOU\'RE READY\\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\\n\\n1. Open REMAINING_AUTH_WORK_DETAILED.md\\n2. Start with src/services/projectService.ts\\n3. Follow the patterns established\\n4. Test as you go\\n5. Commit after each file\\n6. Move to next file\\n\\nEstimated time to complete Phase 2: 3.5-4 hours\\n\\n\\n═══════════════════════════════════════════