2026-01-26 04:29:30.871 | DEBUG    | Model request part: {"content": "Here are information or guidelines specific to this workspace that you should consider when resolving requests:\n<workspace_instruction>\nInstructions for the current directory (these take precedence if relevant):\n\n# Arkan Project - Rovodev Agent Instructions\n\n## Memory Bank Philosophy\n\nI am a Rovodev agent with memory that resets between sessions. The memory bank is my foundational system for retaining project context and accumulated knowledge. I must read and understand the memory bank at the start of every task.\n\n**Critical**: This project has identified **CRITICAL SECURITY VULNERABILITIES** that block production deployment. Security must be the top priority.\n\n## Current Memory Bank Structure\n\n### Core Files (MUST READ ALWAYS)\n\n1. **`memory-bank/README.md`** - Memory bank index and navigation guide\n2. **`memory-bank/projectbrief.md`** - Project overview, goals, and roadmap\n3. **`memory-bank/techContext.md`** - Complete technology stack and configurations\n4. **`memory-bank/activeContext.md`** - **\ud83d\udd34 CRITICAL** - Current work streams, blockers, and security issues\n5. **`memory-bank/systemPatterns.md`** - Architecture patterns and best practices\n6. **`memory-bank/progress.md`** - Development progress and metrics\n7. **`memory-bank/productContext.md`** - Product features, users, and competitive analysis\n8. **`memory-bank/recentUpdates.md`** - Latest changes and changelog\n\n### Reading Priority\n\n**For EVERY task, read in this order:**\n1. `activeContext.md` - Know current blockers and priorities\n2. `systemPatterns.md` - Understand coding patterns\n3. Relevant specific files based on task type\n\n## Memory Bank Usage Rules\n\n### 1. Mandatory Reading at Session Start\n\n**ALWAYS start by reading:**\n- `memory-bank/activeContext.md` - Current priorities and blockers\n- `memory-bank/systemPatterns.md` - Coding patterns to follow\n- Task-specific memory bank files\n\n**Before making ANY changes:**\n- Understand current project context\n- Review existing architecture and patterns\n- Check for related work in progress\n\n### 2. Update Memory Bank When Needed\n\n**Propose updates when:**\n- Learning new important information\n- Making architectural decisions\n- Completing significant milestones\n- Discovering bugs or security issues\n- Changing established patterns\n\n**Update format:**\n- Add date and description to `recentUpdates.md`\n- Update relevant progress in `progress.md`\n- Document decisions in appropriate files\n\n### 3. Use Context in Decisions\n\n**Every decision must:**\n- Align with established architecture patterns\n- Follow coding standards in `systemPatterns.md`\n- Consider security implications (CRITICAL)\n- Maintain test coverage expectations\n- Update documentation as needed\n\n## Core Project Information\n\n### Project Identity\n\n- **Project**: Arkan - AI-Powered Document Generation Platform\n- **Purpose**: Transform document creation from hours to minutes using intelligent AI agents\n- **Status**: \u26a0\ufe0f Beta/Development (v0.1.0) - **BLOCKED for production due to security issues**\n- **Phase**: 75% of Phase 1 complete\n- **Next Milestone**: Production readiness (Security + Testing + Documentation)\n\n### \ud83d\udd34 CRITICAL SECURITY ISSUES (TOP PRIORITY)\n\n**Production is BLOCKED until these are fixed:**\n\n1. **Hardcoded Firebase credentials** in `src/lib/config.ts`\n   - Contains exposed API keys and private keys\n   - IMMEDIATE rotation required\n   \n2. **Service account JSON committed** to repository\n   - File: `docudec-firebase-adminsdk-2maa7-d07a19d3fc.json`\n   - Full admin access exposed\n   - Must be removed from git history\n   \n3. **No environment variable system**\n   - All secrets in source code\n   - Must implement `.env` configuration\n   \n4. **Hardcoded Ollama server URL**\n   - Location: `src/ai/genkit.ts`\n   - Should be environment variable\n\n**When working on ANY task, prioritize security fixes if applicable.**\n\n### Technology Stack (Latest)\n\n**Frontend:**\n- Next.js 15.5.9 (App Router, Server Components)\n- React 18.3.1\n- TypeScript 5.9.3 (strict mode)\n- Tailwind CSS 3.4.19\n- shadcn/ui + Radix UI\n\n**Backend:**\n- Firebase 11.10.0 (Auth, Firestore, Storage, Hosting)\n- Firebase Admin SDK 13.4.0\n\n**AI/ML:**\n- Genkit 1.27.0\n- Ollama (Gemma 2B, Phi3 Mini, Llama3 8B, Qwen 2.5)\n- Model selection by task type\n\n**State Management:**\n- Zustand 4.5.7 (client state)\n- TanStack Query 5.90.19 (server state)\n- Dexie 4.2.1 (IndexedDB for offline)\n\n**UI Components:**\n- TipTap 2.27.2 (rich text editor)\n- Framer Motion 12.28.1 (animations)\n- Lucide React (icons)\n\n**Export:**\n- docx 8.5.0 (Word documents)\n- pptxgenjs 3.12.0 (PowerPoint)\n- jspdf 4.0.0 (PDF)\n\n### Core Architecture Patterns\n\n**Layered Architecture:**\n```\nPresentation (React Components)\n    \u2193\nState Management (Zustand + React Query + Dexie)\n    \u2193\nAPI/Services (Next.js API Routes + Services)\n    \u2193\nBackend (Firebase + Genkit AI)\n```\n\n**Key Patterns:**\n- **Class-based Models** with immutable updates (Project, User, Section)\n- **Hook Factory Pattern** for reusable logic\n- **Service Layer** abstraction over Firebase\n- **AI Flow Pattern** for generation pipelines\n- **Multi-format Export Pipeline** (Markdown \u2192 AST \u2192 Format)\n\n## Project Work Rules\n\n### 1. Respect Existing Architecture\n\n**Before any code changes:**\n- Read `systemPatterns.md` for established patterns\n- Follow folder structure in `techContext.md`\n- Respect design decisions in `activeContext.md`\n- Check for existing similar implementations\n\n**File Organization:**\n```\nsrc/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 app/              # Next.js App Router pages\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 components/       # React components (ui, shared, feature-specific)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 hooks/            # Custom React hooks (core, data, util, report-mode)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 lib/              # Utilities, models, converters\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 services/         # Business logic and API services\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 context/          # React contexts\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 firebase/         # Firebase configuration and hooks\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 types/            # TypeScript type definitions\n```\n\n### 2. Code Quality Standards\n\n**TypeScript:**\n- \u2705 Use strict mode (already enabled)\n- \u2705 Define explicit types for all functions\n- \u2705 Use interfaces for object shapes\n- \u2705 Avoid `any` type (use `unknown` if needed)\n- \u2705 Use Zod for runtime validation\n\n**Code Style:**\n- \u2705 Follow ESLint rules (check `.eslintrc.json`)\n- \u2705 Use functional components with hooks\n- \u2705 Prefer `const` over `let`\n- \u2705 Use early returns for better readability\n- \u2705 Keep functions under 50 lines when possible\n- \u274c Avoid large files (>500 lines) - split them\n\n**Testing:**\n- \u26a0\ufe0f CRITICAL: Test coverage is <20%, must improve\n- \u2705 Write tests for new features\n- \u2705 Use Jest + React Testing Library\n- \u2705 Test API routes with mock Firebase\n- \u2705 Add E2E tests for critical workflows\n\n### 3. Error Handling Patterns\n\n**API Routes:**\n```typescript\n// Use withAuth wrapper\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  return withAuth(async (req, { user, db }) => {\n    try {\n      // Validate with Zod\n      const validated = schema.parse(await req.json());\n      \n      // Business logic\n      const result = await performOperation(validated);\n      \n      // Return typed response\n      return ApiResponse.success(result);\n    } catch (error) {\n      // Centralized error handling\n      return handleError(error);\n    }\n  })(request);\n}\n```\n\n**Components:**\n```typescript\n// Add Error Boundaries (currently missing!)\n<ErrorBoundary fallback={<ErrorFallback />}>\n  <YourComponent />\n</ErrorBoundary>\n```\n\n**Validation:**\n```typescript\n// Always use Zod for input validation\nconst schema = z.object({\n  title: z.string().min(1),\n  content: z.string().optional(),\n});\n\nconst validated = schema.parse(data);\n```\n\n### 4. Performance Best Practices\n\n**Code Splitting:**\n```typescript\n// Lazy load heavy components\nconst TipTapEditor = dynamic(() => import('./Editor'), {\n  ssr: false,\n  loading: () => <EditorSkeleton />\n});\n```\n\n**Memoization:**\n```typescript\n// Use React.memo for expensive components\nexport const ExpensiveComponent = React.memo(({ data }) => {\n  const computed = useMemo(() => expensiveCalc(data), [data]);\n  return <div>{computed}</div>;\n});\n```\n\n**State Management:**\n- \u2705 Use Zustand for client state\n- \u2705 Use React Query for server state\n- \u2705 Use Dexie for offline storage\n- \u274c Don't mix concerns between state managers\n\n**React Query:**\n```typescript\n// Use proper cache configuration\nconst { data } = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['project', id],\n  queryFn: () => api.getProject(id),\n  staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // 5 minutes\n});\n```\n\n## Recent Important Updates\n\n### January 22, 2026 - Comprehensive Review & Memory Bank Initialization\n\n**\u2705 Completed:**\n- Full codebase review (~29,466 lines)\n- Memory bank documentation created (~70KB)\n- Security vulnerabilities identified\n- Architecture patterns documented\n- Technical debt catalogued\n\n**\ud83d\udd34 Critical Findings:**\n- Exposed Firebase credentials in source code\n- Service account JSON committed to repository\n- Test coverage <20%\n- TypeScript compilation errors\n- 60+ console.log statements\n\n### Completed Features (Phase 1)\n\n**Core Platform:**\n- \u2705 AI-powered document generation\n- \u2705 Multi-format export (DOCX, PPTX, PDF)\n- \u2705 Rich text editor (TipTap)\n- \u2705 Template system\n- \u2705 Credit-based payment system\n- \u2705 Multi-language support (English/Arabic RTL)\n- \u2705 Firebase backend integration\n- \u2705 User authentication & profiles\n\n**AI System:**\n- \u2705 Multi-model support (Gemma, Phi3, Llama3, Qwen)\n- \u2705 Task-based model selection\n- \u2705 Context injection system\n- \u2705 Prompt template system (Handlebars)\n- \u2705 Retry logic with exponential backoff\n- \u2705 AI project consultant chat\n\n**Data Models:**\n- \u2705 Class-based models with business logic\n- \u2705 Immutable update patterns\n- \u2705 TypeScript type definitions\n- \u2705 Zod validation schemas\n\n## Work Guidelines by Task Type\n\n### \ud83d\udd10 Working on Security Issues (HIGHEST PRIORITY)\n\n**Before starting:**\n1. Read `activeContext.md` for security blockers\n2. Understand the scope of credential exposure\n3. Plan environment variable migration\n4. Coordinate credential rotation with team\n\n**Implementation:**\n1. Create `.env.example` with all required variables\n2. Update code to use `process.env.VARIABLE_NAME`\n3. Remove hardcoded credentials\n4. Update `.gitignore` to exclude `.env`\n5. Document environment setup in README\n6. Verify no secrets in git history\n\n**Testing:**\n1. Test with environment variables\n2. Verify Firebase connection works\n3. Check all API routes function\n4. Test AI generation with new config\n\n### \ud83c\udd95 Working on New Features\n\n**Planning:**\n1. Read `projectbrief.md` for feature alignment\n2. Check `systemPatterns.md` for patterns to follow\n3. Review existing similar features\n4. Design data models if needed\n\n**Implementation:**\n1. Create feature branch\n2. Implement following established patterns\n3. Add TypeScript types\n4. Add Zod validation\n5. Write tests (unit + integration)\n6. Update documentation\n\n**Files to Update:**\n- Add to `recentUpdates.md`\n- Update `progress.md` completion status\n- Add API docs if creating endpoints\n\n### \ud83d\udc1b Fixing Bugs\n\n**Investigation:**\n1. Reproduce the bug\n2. Check `activeContext.md` for known issues\n3. Review error logs and stack traces\n4. Understand root cause in system context\n\n**Implementation:**\n1. Fix using centralized error handling\n2. Add error boundaries if UI crash\n3. Add validation if input issue\n4. Write regression test\n5. Test edge cases\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Add to `recentUpdates.md`\n- Remove from known issues in `activeContext.md`\n\n### \u26a1 Performance Optimization\n\n**Analysis:**\n1. Use React DevTools Profiler\n2. Check bundle size with `npm run build`\n3. Review React Query cache strategy\n4. Identify heavy components\n\n**Implementation:**\n1. Implement code splitting with `dynamic()`\n2. Add `React.memo` for expensive renders\n3. Use `useMemo` for expensive calculations\n4. Optimize images with Next.js Image\n5. Lazy load heavy libraries\n\n**Verification:**\n- Run Lighthouse audit (target: 90+)\n- Test on slow network\n- Check bundle size reduction\n\n### \ud83e\uddea Adding Tests\n\n**Current Priority:** HIGH (Coverage <20%)\n\n**Test Types:**\n```typescript\n// Unit Tests (Jest)\ndescribe('Project Model', () => {\n  it('should create project with defaults', () => {\n    // Test model logic\n  });\n});\n\n// Integration Tests (API routes)\ndescribe('POST /api/projects', () => {\n  it('should create project with valid data', async () => {\n    // Mock Firebase, test endpoint\n  });\n});\n\n// E2E Tests (Playwright/Cypress)\ntest('user can generate document', async ({ page }) => {\n  // Test full workflow\n});\n```\n\n**Focus Areas:**\n1. Core business logic (models, services)\n2. API routes (especially generation endpoints)\n3. Critical user workflows (auth, generation, export)\n4. Error handling paths\n\n## Continuous Updates\n\n### When to Propose Memory Bank Updates\n\n**Propose updates when:**\n- Adding significant new features\n- Making architectural decisions\n- Solving complex technical problems\n- Changing development patterns\n- Discovering critical bugs\n- Completing major milestones\n- Learning important project insights\n\n**Update Process:**\n1. Identify which memory bank file to update\n2. Propose clear, concise changes\n3. Include date and description\n4. Cross-reference related changes\n5. Verify information accuracy\n\n### Memory Bank Maintenance\n\n**Regular Activities:**\n- Review file contents periodically\n- Update progress status regularly\n- Add important new information\n- Remove outdated or incorrect information\n- Keep security status current\n- Track technical debt\n\n**Quality Standards:**\n- Be specific and concrete\n- Include dates and context\n- Use consistent formatting\n- Link related information\n- Keep it maintainable\n\n## Common Pitfalls to Avoid\n\n### \u274c Anti-Patterns\n\n1. **Ignoring Security**\n   - Don't commit secrets\n   - Don't skip security reviews\n   - Don't use hardcoded credentials\n\n2. **Poor Testing Practices**\n   - Don't skip writing tests\n   - Don't test implementation details\n   - Don't mock everything\n\n3. **Code Quality Issues**\n   - Don't use `any` type\n   - Don't create large files (>500 lines)\n   - Don't leave console.log in production\n   - Don't skip error handling\n\n4. **State Management Mistakes**\n   - Don't mix state management approaches\n   - Don't store server data in Zustand\n   - Don't forget to invalidate queries\n\n5. **Performance Problems**\n   - Don't load all data at once (use pagination)\n   - Don't skip code splitting for heavy components\n   - Don't over-optimize prematurely\n\n### \u2705 Best Practices\n\n1. **Security First**\n   - Always use environment variables\n   - Review Firebase rules regularly\n   - Validate all inputs with Zod\n   - Implement rate limiting\n\n2. **Test-Driven Development**\n   - Write tests for new features\n   - Maintain >70% coverage target\n   - Test error paths\n   - Add E2E tests for critical flows\n\n3. **Clean Code**\n   - Follow established patterns\n   - Keep functions small and focused\n   - Use descriptive names\n   - Add comments for complex logic\n\n4. **Performance Aware**\n   - Implement code splitting\n   - Use proper memoization\n   - Optimize images\n   - Monitor bundle size\n\n5. **Documentation**\n   - Update memory bank with changes\n   - Document API endpoints\n   - Add JSDoc for public functions\n   - Keep README current\n\n## Quick Reference Commands\n\n### Development\n```bash\n# Start development server (Next.js + Genkit)\nnpm run dev\n\n# Start Genkit only\nnpm run genkit:dev\n\n# Run tests\nnpm run test\n\n# Run tests in watch mode\nnpm run test:watch\n\n# Type check\nnpm run typecheck\n\n# Lint code\nnpm run lint\n\n# Build for production\nnpm run build\n```\n\n### Common File Locations\n\n**Configuration:**\n- `next.config.ts` - Next.js configuration\n- `tsconfig.json` - TypeScript configuration\n- `tailwind.config.ts` - Tailwind CSS configuration\n- `firebase.json` - Firebase configuration\n- `.env.local` - Environment variables (create this!)\n\n**Core Code:**\n- `src/app/` - Next.js pages and API routes\n- `src/components/` - React components\n- `src/hooks/` - Custom React hooks\n- `src/lib/` - Utilities and models\n- `src/services/` - Business logic\n\n**Firebase:**\n- `firestore.rules` - Firestore security rules\n- `firestore.indexes.json` - Firestore indexes\n- `storage.rules` - Storage security rules\n\n**Tests:**\n- `jest.config.js` - Jest configuration\n- `jest.setup.js` - Test setup\n- `src/**/__tests__/` - Test files\n\n## Emergency Contacts & Resources\n\n### Critical Issues\n- **Security vulnerabilities**: Immediate team notification\n- **Production outage**: Check Firebase status, review error logs\n- **Data loss**: Check Firestore backups, IndexedDB state\n\n### Documentation\n- Memory Bank: `memory-bank/`\n- API Docs: `src/config/api-docs.ts`\n- Genkit Flows: `src/ai/flows/`\n\n### External Resources\n- [Next.js 15 Docs](https://nextjs.org/docs)\n- [Firebase Docs](https://firebase.google.com/docs)\n- [Genkit Docs](https://firebase.google.com/docs/genkit)\n- [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com)\n\n## Summary\n\nAs a Rovodev agent working on Arkan:\n\n1. **ALWAYS read the memory bank** at the start of every session\n2. **Security is CRITICAL** - address security issues before features\n3. **Follow established patterns** documented in `systemPatterns.md`\n4. **Write tests** to improve coverage from <20% to 70%+\n5. **Update documentation** when making significant changes\n6. **Respect the architecture** and maintain code quality\n7. **Think before acting** - understand context before implementing\n\nThe memory bank ensures work continuity and quality technical decisions. Read it, understand it, update it, and use it to guide every decision.\n\n---\n\n**Memory Bank Last Updated**: January 22, 2026  \n**Agent Instructions Version**: 1.0  \n**Project Status**: Beta - Production Blocked (Security Issues)\n\n</workspace_instruction>\nLocation-specific best practices, tips, and patterns may be found throughout the current workspace in AGENTS.md or AGENTS.local.md files. Before making any changes in a subdirectory, please read the contents of any memory files if present.", "timestamp": "2026-01-26T04:29:30.868028+00:00", "dynamic_ref": "memory_prompt", "part_kind": "system-prompt"}
