)**:\n  41 - [ ] `src/services/projectService.ts` - 60 min\n  42 - [ ] `src/services/transactionService.ts` - 50 min\n  43 - [ ] `src/services/generation-service.ts` - 20 min\n  44 \n  45 **HIGH (Important)**:\n  46 - [ ] `src/app/api/users/[id]/reset-password/route.ts` - 40 min\n  47 - [ ] `src/app/api/admin/users/[id]/reset-password/route.ts` - 40 min\n  48 - [ ] `src/app/manage-users/actions.ts` - 20 min\n  49 \n  50 **MEDIUM (Can defer)**:\n  51 - [ ] `src/services/templateService.ts` (partial) - 15 min\n  52 - [ ] Test files & seed data - 20-30 min\n  53 \n  54 ### By Effort Level\n  55 \n  56 **Low Effort (< 30 min)**:\n  57 - `src/services/generation-service.ts` - INSERT only\n  58 - Test files & cleanup\n  59 \n  60 **Medium Effort (30-60 min)**:\n  61 - Password reset routes (2 files)\n  62 - `src/app/manage-users/actions.ts`\n  63 - `src/services/templateService.ts`\n  64 \n  65 **High Effort (> 60 min)**:\n  66 - `src/services/projectService.ts` - Complex queries\n  67 - `src/services/transactionService.ts` - Pagination, filtering\n  68 \n  69 ### By Complexity\n  70 \n  71 **⭐ (Simple)**:\n  72 - `src/services/generation-service.ts` - Single function\n  73 \n  74 **⭐⭐ (Medium)**:\n  75 - Password reset routes\n  76 - Test file updates\n  77 - `src/app/manage-users/actions.ts`\n  78 \n  79 **⭐⭐⭐ (Complex)**:\n  80 - `src/services/projectService.ts` - Multiple functions, pagination\n  81 - `src/services/transactionService.ts` - Multiple functions, pagination\n  82 \n  83 ---\n  84 \n  85 ## 🚀 Recommended Session Plans\n  86 \n  87 ### Plan A: Fast Track (1 Long Session - 4 hours)\n  88 ```\n  89 Do all 3 critical services + cleanup in one go\n  90 Pros: Everything done quickly\n  91 Cons: Mentally taxing, harder to catch errors\n  92 Recommended for: Experienced developers only\n  93 ```\n  94 \n  95 ### Plan B: Split Sessions (3 Sessions - Recommended)\n  96 ```\n  97 Session 1 (90 min): projectService.ts + transactionService.ts + generation-service.ts\n  98 Session 2 (80 min): Password reset routes + manage-users\n  99 Session 3 (70 min): Cleanup, testing, verification\n 100 \n 101 Pros: Better quality, easier debugging, good for learning\n 102 Cons: Spread across time\n 103 Recommended for: Most developers\n 104 ```\n 105 \n 106 ### Plan C: Gradual (Daily - 5-6 Days)\n 107 ```\n 108 Day 1: projectService.ts\n 109 Day 2: transactionService.ts\n 110 Day 3: API routes\n 111 Day 4: manage-users + cleanup\n 112 Day 5: Testing\n 113 Day 6: Verification\n 114 \n 115 Pros: Very manageable, good for part-time work\n 116 Cons: Context switching, longer overall time\n 117 Recommended for: Busy schedules\n 118 ```\n 119 \n 120 ---\n 121 \n 122 ## 📍 File Location Map\n 123 \n 124 ```\n 125 src/\n 126 ├── services/\n 127 │   ├── projectService.ts ...................... CRITICAL 🚨\n 128 │   ├── transactionService.ts ................. CRITICAL 🚨\n 129 │   ├── generation-service.ts ................. CRITICAL 🚨\n 130 │   ├── templateService.ts .................... MEDIUM 🟠\n 131 │   └── __tests__/\n 132 │       └── generation-service.test.ts ........ MEDIUM 🟠\n 133 │\n 134 ├── app/api/\n 135 │   ├── users/[id]/reset-password/route.ts ... HIGH 🔴\n 136 │   ├── admin/users/[id]/reset-password/route.ts .. HIGH 🔴\n 137 │   └── __tests__/\n 138 │       └── users.test.ts ..................... MEDIUM 🟠\n 139 │\n 140 ├── app/manage-users/\n 141 │   └── actions.ts ............................ HIGH 🔴\n 142 │\n 143 └── lib/db/\n 144     └── seed.ts .............................. DONE ✅\n 145 ```\n 146 \n 147 ---\n 148 \n 149 ## 📊 Work Estimation\n 150 \n 151 ### By File\n 152 \n 153 | File | Lines | Time | Difficulty | Priority |\n 154 |------|-------|------|-----------|----------|\n 155 | projectService.ts | 150 | 60 min | ⭐⭐⭐ | CRITICAL |\n 156 | transactionService.ts | 120 | 50 min | ⭐⭐⭐ | CRITICAL |\n 157 | generation-service.ts | 50 | 20 min | ⭐⭐ | CRITICAL |\n 158 | reset-password routes | 100 | 80 min | ⭐⭐⭐ | HIGH |\n 159 | manage-users/actions.ts | 50 | 20 min | ⭐⭐ | HIGH |\n 160 | templateService.ts | 40 | 15 min | ⭐ | MEDIUM |\n 161 | Test files | 50+ | 20 min | ⭐⭐ | MEDIUM |\n 162 | **TOTAL** | **~560** | **~265 min** | | |\n 163 \n 164 ### By Session (Recommended Plan B)\n 165 \n 166 | Session | Files | Time | Target |\n 167 |---------|-------|------|--------|\n 168 | 1 | 3 services | 90 min | 50% → 75% |\n 169 | 2 | Routes + actions | 80 min | 75% → 90% |\n 170 | 3 | Cleanup + test | 70 min | 90% → 100% |\n 171 | **TOTAL** | **All 11** | **~240 min** | **100%** |\n 172 \n 173 ---\n 174 \n 175 ## 🔄 Conversion Pattern Reference\n 176 \n 177 ### Keep Open While Working\n 178 \n 179 ```typescript\n 180 // PATTERN 1: SELECT Single\n 181 OLD:  const doc = adminDb.collection(\'projects\').doc(id).get();\n 182       const data = doc.data();\n 183 NEW:  const result = await db.select().from(projects).where(eq(projects.id, id));\n 184 \n 185 // PATTERN 2: SELECT Multiple\n 186 OLD:  const snap = adminDb.collection(\'projects\').where(\'userId\', \'==\', uid).get();\n 187       const items = snap.docs.map(d => d.data());\n 188 NEW:  const items = await db.select().from(projects).where(eq(projects.userId, uid));\n 189 \n 190 // PATTERN 3: INSERT\n 191 OLD:  const ref = adminDb.collection(\'projects\').doc();\n 192       await ref.set({ title, userId });\n 193 NEW:  const result = await db.insert(projects).values({ title, userId }).returning();\n 194 \n 195 // PATTERN 4: UPDATE\n 196 OLD:  await adminDb.collection(\'projects\').doc(id).update({ title: newTitle });\n 197 NEW:  await db.update(projects).set({ title: newTitle }).where(eq(projects.id, id));\n 198 \n 199 // PATTERN 5: DELETE\n 200 OLD:  await adminDb.collection(\'projects\').doc(id).delete();\n 201 NEW:  await db.delete(projects).where(eq(projects.id, id));\n 202 \n 203 // PATTERN 6: PAGINATION\n 204 OLD:  .where(\'id\', \'>\', lastId).orderBy(\'createdAt\', \'desc\').limit(10+1)\n 205 NEW:  .where(gt(projects.id, lastId)).orderBy(desc(projects.createdAt)).limit(10+1)\n 206 \n 207 // PATTERN 7: Firestore Batch (projectService, transactionService)\n 208 OLD:  const batch = adminDb.batch();\n 209       batch.set(ref, data);\n 210       batch.update(ref2, data2);\n 211       await batch.commit();\n 212 NEW:  // Just do multiple queries - no batch needed\n 213       await db.insert(table).values(data);\n 214       await db.update(table).set(data2).where(...);\n 215 ```\n 216 \n 217 ---\n 218 \n 219 ## ✅ Completion Checklist\n 220 \n 221 ### Before Starting\n 222 - [ ] Read REMAINING_AUTH_WORK_DETAILED.md (20 min)\n 223 - [ ] Read REMAINING_WORK_EXECUTION_PLAN.md (15 min)\n 224 - [ ] Review patterns above\n 225 - [ ] Have PostgreSQL schema open\n 226 - [ ] Have dev server ready to test\n 227 \n 228 ### For Each File\n 229 - [ ] Identify all `adminDb` references (grep)\n 230 - [ ] Add PostgreSQL imports\n 231 - [ ] Convert each function\n 232 - [ ] Test immediately in dev\n 233 - [ ] Commit changes\n 234 - [ ] Verify no Firebase refs remain\n 235 \n 236 ### After Each Session\n 237 - [ ] Run full test suite\n 238 - [ ] Check console for errors\n 239 - [ ] Verify no Firebase imports remain in modified files\n 240 - [ ] Update progress documentation\n 241 \n 242 ### Final Verification\n 243 - [ ] All 11 files migrated\n 244 - [ ] 0 Firebase references remaining\n 245 - [ ] All tests passing\n 246 - [ ] Full auth flow works\n 247   - [ ] Signup\n 248   - [ ] Login\n 249   - [ ] Logout\n 250   - [ ] Password reset\n 251   - [ ] User profile\n 252   - [ ] Admin functions\n 253 - [ ] No console warnings/errors\n 254 - [ ] Production ready\n 255 \n 256 ---\n 257 \n 258 ## 🧭 Step-by-Step Quick Start\n 259 \n 260 ### First 5 Minutes\n 261 1. Read this file completely\n 262 2. Open REMAINING_AUTH_WORK_DETAILED.md\n 263 3. Skim the patterns section\n 264 \n 265 ### First 30 Minutes\n 266 1. Open Terminal\n 267 2. Run: `grep -n "adminDb\\|adminAuth" src/services/projectService.ts`\n 268 3. Open projectService.ts in editor\n 269 4. Review each function that needs converting\n 270 \n 271 ### First Hour\n 272 1. Add PostgreSQL imports\n 273 2. Convert first function (getProjectsByUserId)\n 274 3. Test in dev server\n 275 4. Verify it works\n 276 \n 277 ### Then Continue\n 278 1. Convert remaining functions one by one\n 279 2. Test after each one\n 280 3. Commit after each function\n 281 4. Move to next file\n 282 \n 283 ---\n 284 \n 285 ## 📞 Common Questions\n 286 \n 287 **Q: Should I do all files at once?**  \n 288 A: No, do one file at a time. Test after each. Easier to debug.\n 289 \n 290 **Q: Which file should I start with?**  \n 291 A: Start with `projectService.ts` - it\'s the pattern setter.\n 292 \n 293 **Q: Can I do these in any order?**  \n 294 A: Critical files first (services), then high priority, then medium.\n 295 \n 296 **Q: How do I test each function?**  \n 297 A: Use dev server + manual testing, or create test files.\n 298 \n 299 **Q: What if I break something?**  \n 300 A: Git commit after each file, can revert easily.\n 301 \n 302 ---\n 303 \n 304 ## 🎯 Success Indicators\n 305 \n 306 **You know you\'re done when**:\n 307 - ✅ No `adminDb` or `adminAuth` in any modified file\n 308 - ✅ All tests pass\n 309 - ✅ Dev server runs without Firebase errors\n 310 - ✅ Can create projects, transactions, reset passwords\n 311 - ✅ Admin functions work\n 312 - ✅ Zero console errors\n 313 \n 314 ---\n 315 \n 316 ## 📈 Progress Milestones\n 317 \n 318 ```\n 319 Start: 50% (4/15 files)\n 320   ↓\n 321 After Services: 75% (8/15 files) - Everything working except password reset\n 322   ↓\n 323 After Routes: 90% (11/15 files) - Full auth system complete\n 324   ↓\n 325 After Cleanup: 100% (15/15 files) - Production ready\n 326 ```\n 327 \n 328 ---\n 329 \n 330 ## 🚀 Launch Checklist\n 331 \n 332 When you\'re 100% done:\n 333 - [ ] Run: `npm run build`\n 334 - [ ] Run: `npm run test`\n 335 - [ ] Run: `npm run lint`\n 336 - [ ] Manual test entire auth flow\n 337 - [ ] Deploy to staging\n 338 - [ ] Deploy to production\n 339 - [ ] Monitor for errors\n 340 \n 341 ---\n 342 \n 343 ## 📞 Help & Support\n 344 \n 345 **If stuck**:\n 346 1. Check REMAINING_AUTH_WORK_DETAILED.md for your specific file\n 347 2. Review patterns above\n 348 3. Check git diff to see what changed\n 349 4. Try reverting last change and re-reading the pattern\n 350 \n 351 **Common errors**:\n 352 - Type mismatch (string vs number IDs) → Use `parseInt(id)`\n 353 - Pagination not working → Check `gt()` and `desc()` imports\n 354 - Firestore refs left → Search for remaining `adminDb` calls\n 355 - Test failures → Mock functions may need updating\n 356 \n 357 ---\n 358 \n 359 ## 📊 Final Summary\n 360 \n 361 **What\'s Done**:\n 362 - ✅ Core authentication system (50%)\n 363 - ✅ Production-ready patterns\n 364 - ✅ User service fully migrated\n 365 - ✅ API service updated\n 366 - ✅ Auth hooks updated\n 367 \n 368 **What\'s Left**:\n 369 - ⚠️ 3 core services (projectService, transactionService, generation-service)\n 370 - ⚠️ Password reset implementation\n 371 - ⚠️ API routes for user management\n 372 - ⚠️ Cleanup and verification\n 373 \n 374 **Time to Complete**:\n 375 - 🕐 Realistic estimate: 3.5-4 hours\n 376 - 📅 Can be done in 1-3 sessions\n 377 - 🎯 Recommended: 3 sessions of 1.5 hours each\n 378 \n 379 ---\n 380 \n 381 ## 🎯 Next Action\n 382 \n 383 **START HERE**: Open `REMAINING_AUTH_WORK_DETAILED.md` and begin with `src/services/projectService.ts`\n 384 \n 385 **Time Now**: Read documentation files first (30 minutes)  \n 386 **Then**: Start converting projectService.ts (60 minutes)  \n 387 **Total Session 1**: ~90 minutes to 75% completion\n 388 \n 389 **Good luck! You\'ve got this! 🚀**\n 390 \n 391 ---\n 392 \n 393 **Files Created**:\n 394 - REMAINING_AUTH_WORK_DETAILED.md (Main reference)\n 395 - REMAINING_WORK_EXECUTION_PLAN.md (Execution guide)\n 396 - REMAINING_WORK_INDEX.md (This file - Navigation guide)\n 397 \n 398 **Status**: Ready to begin Phase 2 ✅\n 399 \n````'}
