isting\\n\\n### Phase 2: Create Collection-Specific Validation Helpers\\n**File:** `src/lib/firebase/validation-helpers.ts` (~300 lines)\\n\\n**Contents:**\\n- Validation functions for each collection (create, update, partial)\\n- Error handling and formatting\\n- Custom validators for complex fields (emails, URLs, enums)\\n- Batch validation utilities\\n\\n### Phase 3: Update DB Helpers to Use Schemas\\n**File Updates:** `src/lib/firebase/db-helpers.ts`\\n\\n- Import schema validators\\n- Add runtime validation before writes\\n- Return type-safe results from helpers\\n- Add validation error handling\\n\\n### Phase 4: Export Schemas for API Routes\\n**File Updates:** `src/lib/firebase/index.ts`\\n\\n- Export all schemas and validators\\n- Centralized access point for API routes\\n- Consistent type definitions across application\\n\\n### Key Features\\n\\n✅ **Centralized**: Single source of truth for all Firestore data validation\\n✅ **Type-Safe**: Full TypeScript inference from Zod schemas\\n✅ **Consistent**: Uniform error handling and validation patterns\\n✅ **Extensible**: Easy to add new collections and validators\\n✅ **Documented**: Comprehensive JSDoc comments and examples\\n✅ **Tested**: Validation functions with clear error messages\\n✅ **Production-Ready**: Enterprise-grade validation patterns\\n\\n### Validation Pattern\\n\\n```typescript\\n// Schema definition\\nexport const NotificationSchema = z.object({\\n  id: z.string().uuid(),\\n  userId: z.string().min(1),\\n  message: z.string().min(1).max(500),\\n  read: z.boolean(),\\n  createdAt: z.string().datetime(),\\n  // ...\\n});\\n\\n// Type inference\\nexport type Notification = z.infer<typeof NotificationSchema>;\\n\\n// Validator function\\nexport function validateNotification(data: unknown): Notification {\\n  return NotificationSchema.parse(data);\\n}\\n\\n// Custom error handling\\nexport class NotificationValidationError extends Error { }\\n```\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n| Aspect | Benefit |\\n|--------|---------|\\n| **Data Integrity** | Runtime validation prevents invalid data in Firestore |\\n| **Error Messages** | Clear, field-specific error messages for debugging |\\n| **Type Safety** | Full TypeScript support with inferred types |\\n| **API Layer** | API routes can use schemas for request validation |\\n| **DB Helpers** | Helpers can validate before writing to Firestore |\\n| **Documentation** | Schemas serve as living API documentation |\\n| **Testing** | Easy to test validation logic with Zod\'s utilities |\\n\\n### Files to Create/Modify\\n\\n**Create:**\\n- `src/lib/firebase/schemas.ts` - All Firestore collection schemas\\n- `src/lib/firebase/validation-helpers.ts` - Collection-specific validators\\n\\n**Modify:**\\n- `src/lib/firebase/db-helpers.ts` - Import and use schema validators\\n- `src/lib/firebase/index.ts` - Export schemas for API routes\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n\\n✅ All Firestore collections have Zod schemas\\n✅ Validation functions cover create, update, partial update\\n✅ Custom error classes for each collection\\n✅ Type-safe inferred types from schemas\\n✅ DB helpers validate data before writes\\n✅ API routes can access schemas centrally\\n✅ TypeScript compilation passes with no errors\\n✅ All validations follow consistent patterns"}', 'logfire.msg': 'running tool: exit_plan_mode', 'logfire.json_schema': '{"type": "object", "properties": {"tool_arguments": {"type": "object"}, "tool_response": {"type": "object"}, "gen_ai.tool.name": {}, "gen_ai.tool.call.id": {}}}', 'logfire.span_type': 'span'}
